{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00614",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 9.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Come in, Mr Subramaniam. The booking says, cough since you painted the house. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.45,
      "end_seconds": 27.5,
      "duration_seconds": 17.05,
      "text": "Yes, doctor, the cough since we painted the house. We did the whole house, you know. Every room. My son-in-law said, Appa, hire a painter, but I said, why pay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.45,
      "end_seconds": 33.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I see. And the cough began when?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.77,
      "end_seconds": 45.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "About three weeks back. Starting the second day of painting, it began. And it will not leave me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.75,
      "end_seconds": 51.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Is it worse at any particular time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.37,
      "end_seconds": 68.28,
      "duration_seconds": 13.91,
      "text": "Worse near the paint fumes, even now. Yesterday I went to the garage, where the old tins are, and I coughed for ten minutes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.41,
      "end_seconds": 73.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Dry cough, or are you bringing up phlegm?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.88,
      "end_seconds": 84.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "Dry mostly. My wife says it sounds like a dog, ha ha. She is very kind like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.01,
      "end_seconds": 91.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Anything else started along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.4,
      "end_seconds": 103.35,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Sneezing, in the first week. A lot. But that has gone now, the sneezing is gone after we opened all the windows."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.52,
      "end_seconds": 113.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "Good. So the cough remains, the sneezing is gone. Now, you are a known asthmatic?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.63,
      "end_seconds": 124.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Yes, asthma since childhood. Also sinus problem, from my thirties. Both, I am carrying for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.26,
      "end_seconds": 130.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "And your inhaler, which one are you using?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.21,
      "end_seconds": 142.69,
      "duration_seconds": 11.48,
      "text": "Budesonide, the brown one. The dose, I think 200 micrograms, maybe? Twice a day. The pharmacist knows better than me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.4,
      "end_seconds": 150.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "We'll confirm with the pharmacy. Any asthma in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.48,
      "end_seconds": 161.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "My mother had it badly. In her last years, she was always using the pump."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.35,
      "end_seconds": 169.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Thank you. And you worked in what field, before retirement?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.76,
      "end_seconds": 178.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Bank manager, thirty-two years. Retired now. My granddaughter says I only watch cricket."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.31,
      "end_seconds": 191.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Fair enough. Let me take your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.25,
      "end_seconds": 214.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "Blood pressure 130 over 84. Pulse 82. Temperature 36.8. Oxygen 96 percent. Breathing rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.97,
      "end_seconds": 224.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "All okay? I check my pressure at home also, with the machine my son bought."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.89,
      "end_seconds": 244.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Yes, all within range. Let me listen to your chest. Deep breaths, mouth open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.18,
      "end_seconds": 261.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "There is a slight wheeze when you breathe out, mainly at the bases."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.46,
      "end_seconds": 270.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Yes, I can hear it a little myself. Like a small whistle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.71,
      "end_seconds": 280.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "My impression is that the paint fumes irritated your lungs, so this is most likely an asthma flare."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.15,
      "end_seconds": 287.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "So the paint was the culprit. I told my wife."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.65,
      "end_seconds": 299.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.15,
      "text": "Likely, yes. I would like to order a lung function test, so we can see how your airways are working now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.53,
      "end_seconds": 306.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Which test is that? The one where we blow into a tube?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.71,
      "end_seconds": 315.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "Exactly that. Blowing hard into a machine, three attempts. Takes ten minutes, at the front clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.16,
      "end_seconds": 320.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "No problem. I am free today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.97,
      "end_seconds": 335.74,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "Good. Now, your options for the cough itself. One, keep the windows open and stay away from the garage and the old tins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.45,
      "end_seconds": 344.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Garage, yes. I will tell my son to clear it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.44,
      "end_seconds": 351.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Two, use your budesonide regularly, morning and evening, even when you feel fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.66,
      "end_seconds": 360.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "I sometimes skip when feeling fine. I will not skip now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.05,
      "end_seconds": 370.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "Three, let the house air out for another week or two before spending long hours in the freshly painted rooms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.58,
      "end_seconds": 380.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "My wife wants to sleep in the guest room anyway, because of the smell. So that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.85,
      "end_seconds": 391.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "Ha. Then four, a damp cloth rather than a dry broom for dust. That is all I need from you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.64,
      "end_seconds": 400.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Understood, doctor. Thank you for the options. I will do one, two, three, and four."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.27,
      "end_seconds": 410.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Good. The nurse will take you to the test room. Take care, Mr Subramaniam."
    }
  ]
}
